WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:03.440
<i>Mash and the gang were
supposed to defeat forest scorpions</i>

00:03.440 --> 00:05.020
<i>for their outdoor class.</i>

00:05.440 --> 00:07.060
<i>By the way, they look like this.</i>

00:08.070 --> 00:11.940
<i>But Silva from Lang dorm
for some reason came to pick a fight.</i>

00:12.740 --> 00:14.240
<i>What will you do, Mash?</i>

00:14.990 --> 00:15.990
Oh?

01:52.290 --> 01:53.800
<i>What the hell is going on?</i>

01:54.090 --> 01:56.010
<i>The difference in magic power is too big.</i>

01:58.970 --> 02:01.760
<i>Shroom Head looks like
he ain't gonna be of any help.</i>

02:02.510 --> 02:04.970
<i>I gotta think. Think.</i>

02:04.970 --> 02:07.310
<i>How can I save that girl?</i>

02:08.600 --> 02:10.810
Hey, now, was that it?

02:10.810 --> 02:12.480
What a letdown.

02:12.480 --> 02:13.320
What'd you say?

02:14.110 --> 02:17.190
I said it's a letdown
if you don't do anything.

02:17.190 --> 02:18.450
You piece of scum.

02:19.950 --> 02:21.120
So now...

02:21.620 --> 02:24.660
I'm willing to give you guys one chance.

02:24.660 --> 02:25.540
Huh?

02:25.540 --> 02:26.580
A chance?

02:26.870 --> 02:28.410
Yeah, that's right.

02:28.960 --> 02:34.550
Endure five hits from my magic,
and I'll leave that girl alone.

02:36.130 --> 02:40.550
Of course, I'll follow the school rules
and bet one silver coin, too.

02:41.050 --> 02:42.140
How about it?

02:42.140 --> 02:44.100
It's not a bad deal, is it?

02:46.220 --> 02:48.100
Hmm? Well?

02:48.100 --> 02:49.230
Not up for it?

02:49.390 --> 02:50.900
That condition is insane!

02:50.900 --> 02:51.730
All right.

02:54.770 --> 02:56.320
You got a deal.

02:57.150 --> 03:00.610
You can't! If you do,
a serious injury won't be the end of it!

03:00.610 --> 03:03.030
I'll be fine. It's only five hits.

03:03.030 --> 03:07.580
What you talkin' about? It's not just you.
For that Mushroom Head over there, too.

03:08.790 --> 03:10.830
He ain't got nothing to do with this!

03:10.830 --> 03:14.130
Oh, yeah? You don't get to decide that.

03:15.880 --> 03:16.840
All right.

03:18.840 --> 03:20.670
I'll take his hits, too.

03:21.180 --> 03:22.840
Can't complain about that, yeah?

03:25.140 --> 03:26.640
What a riot!

03:26.640 --> 03:28.770
Can you endure ten hits?

03:30.270 --> 03:31.230
Spikes...

03:32.310 --> 03:34.810
This is a problem I got myself into.

03:35.480 --> 03:37.020
I'll get through it somehow.

03:42.490 --> 03:44.160
Iron Fist.

03:47.450 --> 03:49.120
<i>This might be bad.</i>

03:52.830 --> 03:54.170
How's that?

03:54.170 --> 03:56.590
You think you can endure ten of these?

04:02.170 --> 04:03.880
Iron Fist!

04:05.720 --> 04:06.800
I'm not done yet!

04:07.220 --> 04:08.430
Three!

04:08.680 --> 04:09.930
Four!

04:10.140 --> 04:10.980
Five!

04:11.480 --> 04:12.310
Six!

04:13.020 --> 04:13.850
Seven!

04:14.350 --> 04:15.190
Eight!

04:15.690 --> 04:16.560
Nine!

04:29.160 --> 04:32.540
<i>Actually, there's a certain boy
threatening me.</i>

04:33.870 --> 04:37.170
<i>I don't know what I should do.</i>

04:39.550 --> 04:41.050
Bet I look like an idiot.

04:41.710 --> 04:43.420
Even I get it.

04:43.920 --> 04:46.590
It all was too good to be true.

04:47.680 --> 04:50.510
But because I'm an idiot...

04:50.970 --> 04:52.770
I can't fully doubt anything.

04:54.600 --> 04:56.600
Like that girl's tears.

04:57.770 --> 04:59.820
I'm surprised you endured it.

04:59.820 --> 05:05.030
As a reward, the last one
will be an extra big one!

05:06.700 --> 05:08.740
Iron Fist!

05:20.790 --> 05:22.760
What a pity.

05:22.760 --> 05:24.840
But did you really think
you could endure—

05:29.850 --> 05:30.680
Ten hits.

05:31.180 --> 05:32.220
You're done.

05:33.470 --> 05:34.520
<i>This guy...</i>

05:43.070 --> 05:43.900
Hey...

05:45.950 --> 05:47.200
that promise...

05:48.570 --> 05:49.450
I ke—

05:52.740 --> 05:53.580
Hmph.

05:53.950 --> 05:55.370
You idiot.

06:00.790 --> 06:03.210
Idiot, idiot, idiot!

06:03.210 --> 06:05.920
Just how stupid can you really be?

06:05.920 --> 06:07.510
Of course you can't stay standing!

06:07.800 --> 06:10.510
I got a clean hit on you with my magic!

06:11.760 --> 06:13.060
Shroom Head...

06:13.560 --> 06:16.180
take that girl, and run.

06:16.730 --> 06:19.770
I'll somehow make everything work.

06:19.770 --> 06:21.020
Iron Fist.

06:25.730 --> 06:28.530
What are you blathering on about?

06:29.910 --> 06:31.320
Shroom Head...

06:31.820 --> 06:33.870
please, take that girl—

06:33.870 --> 06:34.740
What an idiot.

06:35.740 --> 06:39.080
I know you're under my charm spell,

06:39.080 --> 06:41.380
but I didn't think
you'd be this desperate.

06:41.380 --> 06:44.000
Come on, don't say that.

06:44.000 --> 06:46.420
This guy is truly an idiot.

06:46.670 --> 06:49.470
Basically, he's having a delusion!

06:49.470 --> 06:51.800
Does he think he's
the main character or something?

06:52.510 --> 06:54.010
That's so cheesy.

06:54.510 --> 06:59.020
I hate stuffy guys like you.

06:59.940 --> 07:03.270
But, well, seeing you like that
totally cracks me up.

07:05.020 --> 07:08.690
Dissed by the girl
you sacrificed yourself to protect!

07:08.690 --> 07:12.360
This guy is the sorriest excuse for a man!

07:14.620 --> 07:15.580
Huh?

07:19.580 --> 07:21.830
You guys have gone far enough.

07:25.340 --> 07:26.250
Bring it on.

07:26.750 --> 07:29.630
Now it's my turn
to take that ten-hit challenge.

07:33.640 --> 07:35.850
Come at me, scumbag.

07:41.310 --> 07:44.310
I wonder if Mash is all right.

07:44.560 --> 07:45.400
Huh?

07:45.400 --> 07:47.650
He's got to be all right. He's Mash.

07:47.650 --> 07:51.950
That's right! He even bested
that professor during the entrance exams.

07:53.110 --> 07:55.030
There are different types of magic users.

07:55.530 --> 07:58.410
White Mages excel
at scholarship and support magic.

07:58.410 --> 08:00.700
Red Mages excel at combat.

08:01.540 --> 08:04.000
Mash has been facing White Mages so far.

08:04.710 --> 08:08.250
But any Red Mage past their first year
is really tough.

08:08.960 --> 08:11.550
Double-liners are not uncommon.

08:12.050 --> 08:15.550
Among them,
those that equal or surpass Mash...

08:16.180 --> 08:17.350
are a dime a dozen.

08:18.600 --> 08:20.430
Well, well, well.

08:20.430 --> 08:21.810
That's quite a statement.

08:22.180 --> 08:27.770
What really pisses me off
are people like you and this guy...

08:28.320 --> 08:31.650
hypocrites that are weak, but act tough.

08:32.440 --> 08:36.370
Seeing guys like this,
I just wanna completely mess them up,

08:36.370 --> 08:39.580
mess up that disgusting pride
and mentality.

08:39.910 --> 08:43.660
When they realize they were tricked
and are left helpless,

08:43.660 --> 08:46.080
their faces start twisting up.

08:46.500 --> 08:49.340
It totally cracks me up!

08:51.260 --> 08:52.170
Huh?

08:52.170 --> 08:55.590
My clothes are slightly singed
thanks to him.

08:57.180 --> 09:01.470
Don't make a fool of me, you scum!

09:13.400 --> 09:15.320
You think you can win against me?

09:15.650 --> 09:19.450
I earned two gold coins
during my first year!

09:19.780 --> 09:22.950
My base power
is way stronger than you guys!

09:22.950 --> 09:26.540
And you're in high spirits,
saying you'll kill me?

09:28.460 --> 09:31.460
Go ahead and try, you lowlife!

09:33.460 --> 09:36.970
Come on! Come on!
Where'd that energy go?

09:37.380 --> 09:40.220
Go on and kill me!

09:55.280 --> 09:56.820
Triceps Magic...

09:57.610 --> 09:58.450
Ballista Knuckle.

09:59.110 --> 10:01.330
Triceps Magic, huh?

10:01.330 --> 10:02.990
I've never heard that before.

10:03.410 --> 10:05.000
Are you serious?

10:07.210 --> 10:09.460
Don't make me say it again.

10:09.460 --> 10:12.090
Me and you are on...

10:13.250 --> 10:14.710
differ—

10:18.680 --> 10:19.510
Huh?

10:25.100 --> 10:25.930
Wha?

10:29.060 --> 10:35.360
I-I earned two coins last year
as a first-year.

10:38.530 --> 10:42.200
My magic is top-tier
among the second-years.

10:42.200 --> 10:44.620
I have the skill!

11:03.550 --> 11:05.350
<i>Crap, crap, crap!</i>

11:05.350 --> 11:08.020
<i>I absolutely can't win. Me?</i>

11:08.850 --> 11:12.610
<i>No good. I can't stand.
I have no strength in my body.</i>

11:12.610 --> 11:14.520
<i>I can't tolerate one more hit!</i>

11:15.190 --> 11:16.480
<i>What the hell is this guy?</i>

11:32.460 --> 11:34.880
<i>He sat down? Why?</i>

11:35.380 --> 11:36.840
That makes two.

11:36.840 --> 11:37.670
Huh?

11:39.010 --> 11:42.180
You're going to endure ten hits, right?

11:42.680 --> 11:44.050
Show me how much better you are.

11:47.720 --> 11:50.100
You have eight more to go.

12:04.990 --> 12:05.950
Well?

12:06.950 --> 12:08.660
Think you can go for the third hit?

12:09.750 --> 12:11.660
<i>Damn it, this is bad, really bad.</i>

12:11.660 --> 12:13.960
<i>Any more hits ain't good. I'll die!</i>

12:14.500 --> 12:17.500
<i>Something...
I have to come up with some plan.</i>

12:18.090 --> 12:18.920
<i>Something...</i>

12:32.850 --> 12:33.850
Wha...

12:34.480 --> 12:36.060
<i>Its forehead stone is star-shaped.</i>

12:36.940 --> 12:42.530
<i>Perfect! Forest scorpions worth
more than one silver coin exist!</i>

12:43.360 --> 12:47.620
<i>If I can escape while the giant
forest scorpion fights Mushroom Head...</i>

12:53.830 --> 12:55.370
I'm busy right now.

12:55.880 --> 12:56.710
Sorry.

13:01.960 --> 13:03.420
<i>You gotta be kidding me.</i>

13:03.420 --> 13:06.840
<i>I earned two gold coins in my first year!</i>

13:07.600 --> 13:10.180
<i>I can't let them keep mocking me.</i>

13:10.180 --> 13:11.520
Why don't we call it quits?

13:13.520 --> 13:15.440
I kinda feel bad for you.

13:23.490 --> 13:27.660
<i>Crap, crap.
I didn't even imagine Silva losing.</i>

13:27.660 --> 13:29.990
<i>What should I do?
At this rate, I'm gonna be...</i>

13:34.250 --> 13:35.370
I'm sorry.

13:35.370 --> 13:36.960
He made me do it.

13:37.880 --> 13:39.920
I was scared and couldn't disobey.

13:42.000 --> 13:43.340
I truly am sorry.

13:43.840 --> 13:46.260
I'm such a terrible person, aren't I?

13:51.890 --> 13:52.720
It's all right.

13:53.970 --> 13:54.810
Hmph.

13:54.810 --> 13:56.190
<i>Men are total suckers.</i>

13:57.480 --> 13:58.690
Um...

13:58.690 --> 13:59.650
I...

14:00.940 --> 14:01.770
Oof!

14:05.240 --> 14:06.780
...treat everyone equally.

14:12.830 --> 14:15.370
<i>This guy's got some screws loose.</i>

14:17.080 --> 14:19.000
Mash, are you okay?

14:19.000 --> 14:20.330
You're all beat up!

14:20.670 --> 14:21.920
It's nothing.

14:22.550 --> 14:25.380
So you fought that second-year
named Silva after all?

14:25.880 --> 14:26.720
Yeah.

14:26.720 --> 14:28.220
That's amazing, Mash!

14:28.550 --> 14:30.720
You even defeated a star-stone scorpion.

14:30.720 --> 14:32.640
That's two silver coins!

14:32.970 --> 14:34.140
That's amazing!

14:34.140 --> 14:36.270
You went that far just for me.

14:36.310 --> 14:39.060
Aren't you going at a good pace
since you started, Mash?

14:37.230 --> 14:38.600
I'm sorry.

14:38.770 --> 14:40.600
No, thank you.

14:41.020 --> 14:42.860
Let's hurry over to the Nurse's Office!

14:43.440 --> 14:44.690
<i>What an idiot.</i>

14:44.690 --> 14:46.440
<i>That's so cheesy.</i>

14:51.450 --> 14:52.660
Um...

14:53.830 --> 14:55.580
you look pretty banged up.

14:58.460 --> 14:59.790
Are you okay?

15:03.170 --> 15:04.670
Argh!

15:05.130 --> 15:06.050
Eek!

15:06.050 --> 15:08.300
What's wrong with this guy? Freaky!

15:08.420 --> 15:10.840
Help me!

15:11.550 --> 15:12.550
Shroom Head.

15:13.680 --> 15:18.020
Sorry for getting you
caught up in all that.

15:20.440 --> 15:21.270
Thanks, man.

15:23.360 --> 15:24.270
That's not like you.

15:26.150 --> 15:28.650
Yeah? Shut your damn mouth,
or I'll kill you for real!

15:28.650 --> 15:31.780
I totally felt embarrassed as I
squeezed those words out of my mouth!

15:31.780 --> 15:33.450
Give me a break!

15:33.450 --> 15:35.160
I'm not giving a break or anything.

15:35.160 --> 15:35.990
I'll kill you!

15:35.990 --> 15:37.330
You were targeted, Mash.

15:37.750 --> 15:39.960
I overheard something earlier.

15:39.960 --> 15:43.830
Lang is hunting for coins,
and they're mainly targeting Adler.

15:44.460 --> 15:48.090
That second-year named Silva must have
picked a fight with you because of that.

15:48.710 --> 15:49.720
Lang...

15:50.220 --> 15:54.470
Lang dorm is made up
of the upper crust and their cronies.

15:55.050 --> 15:58.100
They're so-called moralists.
They value birthright above all else.

15:58.810 --> 16:02.230
They'll do anything they can
to prevent us nobodies

16:02.480 --> 16:04.940
from getting into the Bureau of Magic.

16:09.030 --> 16:11.070
Looks like it's starting.

16:12.860 --> 16:18.330
The great war for the coins
against Lang's elite, the Magia Lupus!

16:18.870 --> 16:20.750
MAGIA LUPUS

16:22.410 --> 16:23.500
Magia Lupus.

16:24.830 --> 16:28.670
I thought of a story idea like that
back when I was about 12.

16:29.170 --> 16:31.130
HONK

16:33.680 --> 16:34.510
I see.

16:36.050 --> 16:36.890
Hmm?

16:41.310 --> 16:45.150
One from Pierced Eyebrow
and two from the giant scorpion.

16:45.520 --> 16:47.860
With five silvers,
I finally have a gold coin.

16:49.190 --> 16:50.230
Whoa.

16:50.230 --> 16:53.780
That light makes your face—

16:54.660 --> 16:56.070
My eyes!

16:56.910 --> 16:59.330
Wait, I didn't know we had separate dorms.

16:59.330 --> 17:01.750
Of course we were separated.

17:01.750 --> 17:05.040
You know we were sorted
right after entering, right?

17:05.960 --> 17:07.750
Oh. Now that you mention it...

17:09.750 --> 17:13.050
We will now sort the new students
into their dorms.

17:13.420 --> 17:17.050
Touch the unicorn's horn,
and through your magic power,

17:17.050 --> 17:21.060
it will read your thoughts and ideas
to select a dorm that suits you.

17:21.560 --> 17:23.310
First up, Egalt Vansom.

17:23.810 --> 17:24.810
Here.

17:27.690 --> 17:29.060
Mm-hmm.

17:29.570 --> 17:33.820
I sense willingness in you
and wisdom to match.

17:34.110 --> 17:36.950
You are most suited for...

17:38.450 --> 17:39.700
Orca dorm.

17:39.700 --> 17:40.950
All right!

17:40.950 --> 17:43.200
- Thank you very much!
- Next, Alben Smith.

17:43.200 --> 17:44.330
Here.

17:44.580 --> 17:45.790
Mm-hmm.

17:45.790 --> 17:47.960
Dauntless courage and a pioneering spirit.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.840
It's Adler dorm for you.

17:49.840 --> 17:54.260
Hmm. You have strong magical power,
radical ideas, and a challenging nature.

17:54.260 --> 17:56.220
You belong in Lang dorm.

17:58.300 --> 18:01.970
<i>Heh. Centuries have passed
since I was given this role.</i>

18:01.970 --> 18:06.770
<i>Not once have I misjudged,
as I can read people's thoughts.</i>

18:06.770 --> 18:08.900
- Now, keep them coming!
- Next, Mash Burnedead.

18:09.270 --> 18:10.110
'Kay.

18:19.320 --> 18:22.580
Oh, I need to control my power. Sorry.

18:23.080 --> 18:23.910
<i>Freaky.</i>

18:24.120 --> 18:26.540
<i>Wait, he's only thinking
about cream puffs.</i>

18:26.540 --> 18:27.580
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

18:27.580 --> 18:30.000
<i>Isn't there anything
other than cream puffs?</i>

18:30.290 --> 18:34.510
<i>Seriously, what are you thinking about?
What's with that face?</i>

18:34.960 --> 18:39.430
<i>No, this is bad. Several centuries
into dorm selection at our academy,</i>

18:39.430 --> 18:42.930
<i>not once have I
been stumped for an answer.</i>

18:44.010 --> 18:45.430
<i>Okay, let's try this again.</i>

18:47.430 --> 18:48.350
<i>Bliss.</i>

18:50.940 --> 18:54.820
A cream puff is a confection
where batter is baked into a hollow shell

18:54.820 --> 18:57.990
and custard cream is packed
into the empty space inside.

18:57.990 --> 19:01.240
Especially for Choux Au Craquelin,
where gooey cream fills a brittle shell.

19:01.240 --> 19:02.780
And if one were to make an analogy
with humans, it's someone

19:02.780 --> 19:05.160
- harboring kindness within strength—
- It's suddenly gotten eloquent!

19:05.740 --> 19:08.790
Cream puff lovers go to Adler!

19:08.790 --> 19:10.790
That... was a leap of logic!

19:11.580 --> 19:12.420
'Kay.

19:13.670 --> 19:15.380
Oh, yeah, there was that.

19:16.300 --> 19:17.380
<i>So that was...</i>

19:17.380 --> 19:18.380
<i>- Mash.
- This guy.</i>

19:18.380 --> 19:19.550
<i>I see.</i>

19:19.800 --> 19:20.890
Ahem.

19:21.390 --> 19:24.180
Lang's elite, the Magia Lupus,

19:24.180 --> 19:26.930
are a group
of seven distinguished students.

19:27.520 --> 19:29.940
That Pierced Eyebrow
must be one of their lackeys.

19:30.440 --> 19:33.560
They've been grabbing up coins
to sway who the Divine Visionary will be.

19:33.560 --> 19:35.940
Since you have a coin...

19:36.400 --> 19:42.360
keep your distance from Lang,
and stick with dormmates whenever you can.

19:42.950 --> 19:44.660
Okay. I will.

19:45.240 --> 19:48.200
<i>But Lance's warning was in vain...</i>

19:48.660 --> 19:50.920
<i>and Mash found himself lost in school.</i>

19:51.830 --> 19:54.040
Where's the next class?

19:56.920 --> 19:58.420
Here it is, I think.

19:59.050 --> 20:01.680
Should I push or pull to open this door?

20:02.550 --> 20:03.390
Hmm.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.220
I always get it wrong.

20:07.350 --> 20:11.190
Do I push or pull? Hmm...

20:12.600 --> 20:14.100
I-I'm sorry!

20:14.100 --> 20:15.690
I'm terribly sorry!

20:15.690 --> 20:18.650
Look, you said you wanted to join us,

20:18.650 --> 20:21.990
and that's why Lord Abel
gave you a chance.

20:22.280 --> 20:25.160
Furthermore, you let Adler take a coin.

20:25.160 --> 20:28.200
O-Once more! Please give me one more chan—

20:28.200 --> 20:29.160
You misunderstand.

20:29.660 --> 20:30.500
Huh?

20:30.830 --> 20:32.830
I gave a chance?

20:33.620 --> 20:36.840
That makes it sound
like I expected something out of him.

20:37.750 --> 20:39.880
Oh, man, sorry 'bout that.

20:40.210 --> 20:42.880
Humans worthy
of making this world go round...

20:43.380 --> 20:45.590
must be chosen individuals.

20:46.430 --> 20:51.600
Perfect education.
Overwhelming talent. Noble bloodline.

20:53.390 --> 20:58.020
We're collecting coins
to create a world free of impurities.

20:58.770 --> 21:00.400
But what about you?

21:02.440 --> 21:05.240
You can't even become
a sacrificial pawn for our objective.

21:06.160 --> 21:08.450
Pathetic wretch. You have my sympathy.

21:08.950 --> 21:12.910
It must be hard to go on living,
knowing that you're worthless.

21:14.420 --> 21:15.670
But rest assured.

21:18.590 --> 21:21.630
You no longer need to think
about such things.

21:32.890 --> 21:35.640
The Divine Visionary should be me.

21:36.230 --> 21:38.230
Not some riffraff from Adler.

21:40.610 --> 21:41.780
Right...

21:42.110 --> 21:43.070
Mother?

21:44.700 --> 21:46.740
A world free of impurities.

21:47.490 --> 21:48.320
It will be my—

21:49.330 --> 21:50.280
Um...

21:51.950 --> 21:54.580
I couldn't figure out
whether to push or pull this door open.

21:54.580 --> 21:55.410
Sorry.

